Snake and Ladder Game — Complete LLD in Java with Explanation
This combines the requirements slide, all the Java screenshots (Player, Dice, Jumper, GameBoard), and your handwritten notes about startGame(), player turns, dice rolls, snakes, ladders, and winning conditions.

The implementation below follows the same approach as your notes, with a few corrections to make the game work reliably.
1. Requirements
- Multiplayer game.
- Configurable board size.
- Configurable snake and ladder positions.
- Configurable number of dice.
- Every player starts at position 0.
- Players take turns in a queue.
- A player rolls the dice and moves forward.
- Landing on a snake moves the player down; landing on a ladder moves them up.
- A player wins by reaching the final cell exactly.
- If a move exceeds the board size, the player stays in their current position and their turn ends.
2. Class design
GameBoard

Coordinates turns, positions, snakes, ladders and the game loop

Dice

Rolls the configured number of dice



Player

Player ID and name


Jumper

Start and end positions for snakes and ladders




The GameBoard stores:
- Dice dice — the dice configuration.
- Queue<Player> nextTurn — the next player's turn.
- List<Jumper> snakes — snake configurations.
- List<Jumper> ladders — ladder configurations.
- Map<Integer, Integer> playersCurrentPosition — player ID mapped to current position.
- int boardSize — the final cell number.
3. Complete Java code
Put the following code in a file named SnakeAndLadder.java. It uses nested classes so that you can compile and run the entire implementation as one file. In a project matching your screenshots, you can later split these classes into separate files.

import java.util.*;

// Run with: javac SnakeAndLadder.java && java SnakeAndLadder
public class SnakeAndLadder {

    // -------------------- Player --------------------
    static class Player {
        private final String playerName;
        private final int id;

        Player(String playerName, int id) {
            this.playerName = Objects.requireNonNull(playerName);
            this.id = id;
        }

        String getPlayerName() {
            return playerName;
        }

        int getId() {
            return id;
        }
    }

    // -------------------- Dice --------------------
    static class Dice {
        private final int numberOfDice;
        private final Random random = new Random();

        Dice(int numberOfDice) {
            if (numberOfDice <= 0) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "Number of dice must be positive");
            }
            this.numberOfDice = numberOfDice;
        }

        int rollDice() {
            int total = 0;
            for (int i = 0; i < numberOfDice; i++) {
                total += random.nextInt(6) + 1;
            }
            return total;
        }
    }

    // -------------------- Jumper --------------------
    static class Jumper {
        private final int startPoint;
        private final int endPoint;

        Jumper(int startPoint, int endPoint) {
            this.startPoint = startPoint;
            this.endPoint = endPoint;
        }

        int getStartPoint() {
            return startPoint;
        }

        int getEndPoint() {
            return endPoint;
        }
    }

    // -------------------- GameBoard --------------------
    static class GameBoard {
        private final int boardSize;
        private final Dice dice;
        private final Queue<Player> nextTurn = new ArrayDeque<>();
        private final Map<Integer, Integer> playersCurrentPosition =
            new HashMap<>();
        private final Map<Integer, Integer> snakes = new HashMap<>();
        private final Map<Integer, Integer> ladders = new HashMap<>();
        private boolean gameOver = false;

        GameBoard(int boardSize, Dice dice, List<Player> players,
                  List<Jumper> snakeList, List<Jumper> ladderList) {
            if (boardSize < 2 || dice == null || players == null ||
                    players.size() < 2 ||
                    snakeList == null || ladderList == null) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid game setup");
            }

            this.boardSize = boardSize;
            this.dice = dice;

            Set<Integer> ids = new HashSet<>();
            for (Player player : players) {
                if (player == null || !ids.add(player.getId())) {
                    throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                        "Players must have unique IDs");
                }
                nextTurn.offer(player);
                playersCurrentPosition.put(player.getId(), 0);
            }

            configureJumpers(snakeList, snakes, true);
            configureJumpers(ladderList, ladders, false);

            for (Integer start : snakes.keySet()) {
                if (ladders.containsKey(start)) {
                    throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                        "Snake and ladder cannot start at the same cell");
                }
            }
        }

        private void configureJumpers(List<Jumper> jumpers,
                                      Map<Integer, Integer> map,
                                      boolean isSnake) {
            for (Jumper jumper : jumpers) {
                if (jumper == null) {
                    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Null jumper");
                }

                int start = jumper.getStartPoint();
                int end = jumper.getEndPoint();

                boolean validDirection =
                    isSnake ? start > end : start < end;

                if (start < 1 || start >= boardSize ||
                        end < 1 || end > boardSize ||
                        !validDirection || map.containsKey(start)) {
                    throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                        "Invalid snake/ladder: " + start + " -> " + end);
                }

                map.put(start, end);
            }
        }

        void startGame() {
            while (!gameOver && !nextTurn.isEmpty()) {
                Player player = nextTurn.poll();

                int currentPosition =
                    playersCurrentPosition.get(player.getId());
                int diceValue = dice.rollDice();
                int nextCell = currentPosition + diceValue;

                System.out.println("\n" + player.getPlayerName()
                    + " rolled " + diceValue);

                if (nextCell > boardSize) {
                    System.out.println("Move exceeds board; turn skipped.");
                    nextTurn.offer(player);
                    continue;
                }

                int finalPosition = nextCell;

                if (snakes.containsKey(nextCell)) {
                    finalPosition = snakes.get(nextCell);
                    System.out.println("Snake! Down to " + finalPosition);
                } else if (ladders.containsKey(nextCell)) {
                    finalPosition = ladders.get(nextCell);
                    System.out.println("Ladder! Up to " + finalPosition);
                }

                playersCurrentPosition.put(
                    player.getId(), finalPosition);

                System.out.println(player.getPlayerName()
                    + " is at position " + finalPosition);

                if (finalPosition == boardSize) {
                    System.out.println(
                        player.getPlayerName() + " won the game!");
                    gameOver = true;
                } else {
                    nextTurn.offer(player);
                }
            }
        }

        Map<Integer, Integer> getPlayerPositions() {
            return Collections.unmodifiableMap(
                new HashMap<>(playersCurrentPosition));
        }
    }

    // -------------------- Main --------------------
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int boardSize = 100;
        int numberOfDice = 1;

        List<Player> players = Arrays.asList(
            new Player("Alice", 1),
            new Player("Bob", 2),
            new Player("Charlie", 3)
        );

        List<Jumper> snakes = Arrays.asList(
            new Jumper(99, 10),
            new Jumper(75, 35),
            new Jumper(45, 15)
        );

        List<Jumper> ladders = Arrays.asList(
            new Jumper(4, 25),
            new Jumper(13, 46),
            new Jumper(50, 80)
        );

        GameBoard game = new GameBoard(
            boardSize, new Dice(numberOfDice),
            players, snakes, ladders
        );

        game.startGame();
    }
}



