7. Time and space complexity
Let:
- \(P\) = number of players.
- \(S\) = number of snakes.
- \(L\) = number of ladders.
- \(D\) = number of dice.
Operation	Complexity
Initialize players	\(O(P)\)
Configure snakes and ladders	\(O(S+L)\) average
Roll all dice	\(O(D)\)
Look up a snake or ladder	\(O(1)\) average
Update a player's position	\(O(1)\) average
Process one turn	\(O(D)\) average

The game uses \(O(P+S+L)\) space for player state and the configured snakes and ladders, excluding the small amount of temporary memory used during a turn.

The total game duration depends on the number of turns needed to reach the winning cell.
